# Gwent Project Task Management

## Task Numbering System

All tasks must follow a strict numbering system:
- Tasks use a 3-digit prefix starting at 000
- Each task has a unique number
- Numbers are assigned sequentially
- Example: Task 000, Task 001, Task 002, etc.
- Task 000 is the root task and starting point of the project
- All other tasks must be descendants of Task 000
- The task tree must form a single connected graph with Task 000 as the root

## Task Dependencies

Each task must explicitly track its dependencies using task IDs:
- Dependencies should be listed in the task description
- Use the full task ID (e.g., "000") when referencing dependencies
- The dependency tree will be used to determine task execution order
- Circular dependencies are strictly prohibited
  - No task can depend on itself
  - No task can depend on another task that directly or indirectly depends on it
  - All dependencies must form a directed acyclic graph (DAG)
  - Dependencies should be validated before task creation or modification
- Every task except Task 000 must have at least one dependency
- All tasks must be reachable from Task 000 through the dependency tree

