## Task Categories

1. **Design Tasks** (000-099)
   - System architecture
   - Component design
   - Interface specifications

2. **Evaluation Tasks** (100-199)
   - Technology evaluation
   - Performance testing
   - Security assessment

3. **Decision Tasks** (200-299)
   - Technology selection
   - Architecture decisions
   - Implementation approaches

4. **Implementation Tasks** (300-399)
   - Hardware implementation
   - Software development
   - Integration testing

## Task Status Indicators

- 🔴 Not Started
- 🟡 In Progress
- ⚫ Blocked
- 🟢 Completed

## Priority Levels

- 🔴 High
- 🟡 Medium
- 🟢 Low

## Standard Task Format

```
### Task XXX: Task Title
- Description: Detailed task description
- Priority: [High|Medium|Low]
- Status: [Not Started|In Progress|Blocked|Completed]
- Dependencies: [Task IDs]
- File: [design/[TaskID]-[description].md](design/[TaskID]-[description].md)
```

## Task Tracking Files

- All tasks have their own files in the `design` folder
- File names must be Linux-compatible (no spaces, special characters)
- The Task ID must be used as the filename prefix
  - Example: Task 000 should be in file [design/000-product-requirements.md](mdc:design/000-product-requirements.md)
  - Example: Task 001 should be in file [design/001-hardware-requirements.md](mdc:design/001-hardware-requirements.md)
- The filename format is: [design/[TaskID]-[description].md](design/[TaskID]-[description].md)
  - TaskID must match exactly (e.g., "000")
  - Description should be in kebab-case (lowercase with hyphens)

